content.thinking:
No dedicated core_test.go. The refactor: extract shared per-victim judgment into one function used by both `Detect` and `DetectBlockWithRules`. 

Design: add to core.go (or replay.go) a function like:

```go
// judgment is the shared per-victim conclusion of the sandwich and
// displacement rules, before evidence is attached.
type judgment struct {
    kind     string
    severity int
}

// judgeSwap applies the sandwich and displacement rules to one victim swap
// and its adjacent neighbours inside its own pool...
func judgeSwap(front, victim, back Swap, hasBack bool, rules RuleSet) (judgment, bool)
```

Actually simpler: pass pointers like DetectBlockWithRules does:

```go
func judgeVictim(front, back *Swap, victim Swap, rules RuleSet) (kind string, severity int, hit bool) {
    if rules.Sandwich.Enabled && front != nil && back != nil &&
        front.Trader == back.Trader && front.Trader != victim.Trader &&
        front.GasPrice > victim.GasPrice && back.GasPrice > victim.GasPrice {
        return "sandwich", rules.Sandwich.Severity, true
    }
    if rules.Displacement.Enabled && front != nil &&
        gasDominates(front.GasPrice, victim.GasPrice, int64(rules.Displacement.Multiplier)) {
        return "displacement", rules.Displacement.Severity, true
    }
    return "", 0, false
